course: dictionary
lesson: 2953
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. You find out which meaning you need by reading the words around it. These words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes, a driver delivers and a shopkeeper sells.» Here a driver is the person who drives the van that brings the bread. The clue is delivers, which is what the driver does.
explain: «You never ride up the inside of a lorry or truck at a junction, because the driver cannot see you.» The driver here is the person who drives the lorry. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the person who drives the lorry cannot see you" makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Some meanings are not about people at all. In golf, a driver is a club for long shots. For a computer, a driver is a program. Look at the words beside it, like golf or device, to find the right meaning.
fact: A driver is a person who drives a car, bus, truck or train.
fact: «Bus drivers help you get on and off safely.»
fact: Wait until the driver sees you and stops before you cross the road.
fact: A device driver is a program that helps a computer use a device.
fact: A driver can also be something that makes something else happen, as in «a driver of change».
exercise: «You never ride up the inside of a lorry or truck at a junction, because the driver cannot see you.» What does driver mean here? | A golf club for long shots | Something that makes change happen | *The person who drives the lorry or truck | A program that helps a computer work
exercise: In golf, what is a driver? | A bag for carrying golf balls | *A golf club used for long shots | A person who drives a golf buggy
exercise: What is a device driver? | *A program that helps a computer use a device | A person who fixes printers | A lorry for carrying goods | Something that makes change happen
test: «Bus drivers help you get on and off safely.» In this sentence, driver means? | A computer program | A golf club | Someone who sells bread | *A person who drives a bus
test: «a driver of change» — what does driver mean here? | A golf club | A person who drives a taxi | *Something that makes change happen | A computer program
exam: In the bread sentence, what is the driver's job? | Selling bread in a shop | Grinding flour | *Delivering the bread | Growing wheat
